 - Every Gradle run needs Maven Central, even offline-looking ones: `build.gradle` resolves Jersey transitive versions at configuration time. The fast gate is offline only once the Gradle cache is warm.
 
+## 2026-11-02: JMAK commands over TCP and SMS
+
+Added `JmakProtocolEncoder` with a `textChannel` flag: false for the TCP channel (`$id;value;|...#`), true for SMS (`JMAK#action;id;value#...#`, and `JMAK#REBOOT#` for reboot). `JmakProtocol` declares the same 12 commands for data and text and registers the encoder on both channels. Added `Command.TYPE_ALARM_MOVEMENT` ("alarmMovement") because no movement alarm type existed. Tests: `JmakProtocolEncoderTest` covers every command over TCP and SMS, plus one run through the production handler order.
+
+Learned: in the TCP pipeline, `NetworkMessageHandler` unwraps `NetworkMessage` before a `StringEncoder` placed in the protocol handlers can see the output, so a String from the encoder would reach the socket unencoded. The TCP encoder therefore returns an ASCII `ByteBuf`. `BaseProtocol` sends the custom command through the encoder only when its type is in the supported data commands, so custom is listed there.
+
+Left: power removal alarm is mapped to the existing `alarmRemove` type and the movement alarm to the new `alarmMovement` type; both mappings need a human check. The odometer value is sent as given in the command data, with no unit conversion. No test against a real JMAK device.
+
